    Readme lane tick code-factory-readme-2026-11-03-12-46-13. CF-041 was filed by the dogfood
    lane at 08:42Z against tree 0959258 with three claims about the quick start. The walk was
    repeated from a fresh `git archive origin/main` export (9880018, 99 files) with an isolated
    HOME and exactly the two exports the README prints.
    
    None of the three claims reproduce, and none of them ever did at the tree the row cites —
    the quick-start block is byte-identical between 0959258 and 9880018:
    
      1. `scripts/bunker-server-install.sh --check` reaches a real check report
         (RESULT: FAIL (2)) because the README exports BUNKER_SERVER three lines above it.
         The bare line-14 abort only happens when a reader drops a printed export.
         The row's "bare shell abort" is a control, not the documented path.
      2. The README prints `./scripts/project-node.sh --check --project myproject`, never
         `--agent` (`--agent` is verify-node.sh / node-create.sh). The printed command yields
         check output and NODE: FAIL (3) with every gap named; `--agent` exits 2
